DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260810
SUMMARY:Deadline: Red Quincho: Beca Constelaciones 2026 (4th Edition)
DESCRIPTION:Beca Constelaciones is Red Quincho's mobility and production gr
 ant for artists\, curators and researchers doing territory-based work\, no
 w in its fourth edition. Each recipient spends one month in residence\, sp
 lit into two 15-day placements at different member spaces across Argentina
 \, pairing an urban and a rural context. The grant covers mobility\, livin
 g costs and production\, with lodging provided. Backed by Fundacion Willia
 ms\, CCEBA and Fundacion Santander through the CABA Mecenazgo scheme. ELIG
 IBILITY IS RESTRICTED: of the 15 grants\, 13 are for people resident in Ar
 gentina and 2 are for people currently living in Spain. Artists\, curators
  and researchers apply through separate forms\; Spanish-based candidates f
 ace an additional jury evaluation. Deadline 9 August 2026 at 23:59 Argenti
 na time.\n\nOrganisation: Red Quincho\nLocation: Rotating urban and rural 
 Red Quincho spaces across Argentina\; residency runs September to December
  2026.\nAward: ARS 1\,000\,000 (around USD 690) per grant toward mobility\
 , living costs and production\, plus one month of lodging. 15 grants avail
 able. No application fee.\nDuration: One-month residency split into two 15
 -day placements at different spaces.\n\nMore: https://redquincho.ar/beca-c
 onstelaciones-2026/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
URL:https://redquincho.ar/beca-constelaciones-2026/?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Rotating urban and rural Red Quincho spaces across Argentina\; res
 idency runs September to December 2026.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ramdam-extended-possibilities-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260901T124023Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260714
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260715
SUMMARY:Deadline: RAMDAM\, un centre d'art: Extended Possibilities Residenc
 y 2027
DESCRIPTION:Extended Possibilities gives artists the opportunity to work on
  site at RAMDAM\, un centre d'art for 45 days\, a long period allowing the
 m to benefit from technical support and to present ongoing work to the pub
 lic. Artists receive on-site accommodation (a collective room for the whol
 e 45 days)\, access to a well-maintained\, up-to-date technical facility\,
  a grant to support their work\, and a lump-sum allowance for travel and v
 isas. RAMDAM is an activist space supporting artists in their artistic res
 earch\; residencies are open to artists or teams engaged in creation\, res
 earch\, or experimentation\, with no obligation to produce a finished work
 : dance\, theatre\, performance\, painting\, sculpture\, drawing\, film\, 
 video\, literary writing\, screenwriting\, digital art\, and hybrid forms 
 are all welcome. The call focuses on multidisciplinary projects and resear
 ch that break down barriers between disciplines and challenge their own fi
 eld of practice\, and considerable attention is given to how the work fits
  into a social and/or political context and resonates with our times. THE 
 CALL SUPPORTS: 1 or 2 artistic teams (RAMDAM can host at most 5 artists)\;
  performing artists of all disciplines\; projects at early stages of resea
 rch-creation and/or more advanced (residencies can be writing residencies 
 and/or stage residencies). All artists must be available for the full 45 d
 ays from 1 February to 15 March 2027 and must be from eligible countries (
 EU countries\, outermost regions\, overseas countries and territories\, an
 d some non-EU countries)\; artists from mainland (hexagonal) France cannot
  apply. The working and living spaces are wheelchair accessible\, though r
 eaching RAMDAM by public transport can be difficult for disabled people\; 
 accessibility support is available via Culture Moves Europe for residents 
 with disabilities. ALLOWANCES: EUR 1\,350 per resident for subsistence\; t
 ravel allowance EUR 400 under 5\,000 km or EUR 800 from 5\,000 km (travel 
 under 600 km must be by green means of transport unless disability or isla
 nd residence requires otherwise)\; green mobility top-up EUR 400 per resid
 ent for non-plane travel over 600 km\; visa top-up EUR 120\; outermost reg
 ions/OCT top-up EUR 175\; family top-up EUR 200 per child under 18 (housin
 g capacity is limited). TO APPLY: applications in English or French\; down
 load the residency project and administrative form documents and email the
  complete application to contact@ramdamcda.org with subject line 'extended
  possibilities - 2027' (no WeTransfer\, no important information in the em
 ail body\; reduce file sizes\; a third document may be added to help under
 stand the work). Confirmation within 7 working days\; shortlisted applican
 ts have video calls with the residency committee in mid-August. Deadline: 
 Tuesday 14 July 2026\, 11:59 p.m. NOTE: the call is arbitrarily limited to
  the first 40 applications received (still open as of 1 July 2026)\, so ap
 ply early. Made possible by the European programme Culture Moves Europe.\n
 \nOrganisation: RAMDAM\, un centre d'art\nLocation: Sainte-Foy-les-Lyon (n
 ear Lyon)\, France\; open to artists legally resident in Culture Moves Eur
 ope eligible countries (EU member states\, outermost regions\, overseas co
 untries and territories\, and some non-EU countries)\; artists from mainla
 nd (hexagonal) France cannot apply\nAward: EUR 1\,350 per resident allowan
 ce for subsistence and other costs\, plus travel allowance of EUR 400 (und
 er 5\,000 km) or EUR 800 (from 5\,000 km). Top-ups: green mobility EUR 400
  per resident (600 km or more by non-plane transport)\, visa EUR 120\, out
 ermost regions/OCT EUR 175\, family EUR 200 per child under 18. On-site ac
 commodation and technical facilities provided. Supported by Culture Moves 
 Europe.\nDuration: 45 days\, 1 February to 15 March 2027\n\nMore: https://
 ramdamcda.org/actualite-ramdam/extended-possibilities-residency-call?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ramdamcda.org/actualite-ramdam/extended-possibilities-residency
 -call?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Sainte-Foy-les-Lyon (near Lyon)\, France\; open to artists legally
  resident in Culture Moves Europe eligible countries (EU member states\, o
 utermost regions\, overseas countries and territories\, and some non-EU co
 untries)\; artists from mainland (hexagonal) France cannot apply
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jentel-artist-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124023Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Jentel Artist Residency
DESCRIPTION:The Jentel Artist Residency offers approximately three-week res
 idencies in the foothills of the Bighorn Mountains near Banner\, Wyoming\,
  giving artists\, writers\, and composers dedicated time for creative work
 . Sessions run from mid-January through early December\, hosting six resid
 ents at a time. It is open to visual artists in any medium\, writers of fi
 ction\, creative nonfiction\, or poetry\, and composers across musical gen
 res. Residents receive a private bedroom\, a separate studio\, shared livi
 ng and kitchen space\, and a USD 100 weekly stipend to help cover food and
  personal expenses. Applicants must be at least 25 years old and be U.S. c
 itizens or foreign nationals whose primary residence is in the U.S. during
  the application year\, and may not be enrolled full-time in a degree prog
 ram. There is a USD 30 non-refundable application fee\, with deadlines of 
 September 15 for Winter and Spring sessions and January 15 for Summer and 
 Fall sessions.\n\nOrganisation: Jentel Foundation\nLocation: Banner\, Wyom
 ing\, USA\nAward: USD 100 weekly stipend (about USD 300 total over three w
 eeks)\, plus private bedroom\, separate studio space\, and shared living a
 nd kitchen facilities provided at no cost USD 30 application fee\nDuration
 : Approximately 3 weeks (arrive on the 15th\, depart the morning of the 7t
 h of the following month)\n\nMore: https://www.jentelarts.org/apply?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.jentelarts.org/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Banner\, Wyoming\, USA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:simons-foundation-open-interval-turbulence-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124023Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Open Interval: An Artist-Scientist Exploration of Turbule
 nce
DESCRIPTION:Open Interval is a Simons Foundation program that supports trio
 s consisting of an artist\, a scientist\, and a representative from a 501(
 c)(3) arts organization to collaborate around a shared scientific theme. T
 he current cycle centers on the theme of turbulence\, a phenomenon at the 
 edge of chaos and beauty. Awarded trios receive USD 30\,000 to support a s
 ustained period of thought partnership and exploration rather than the pro
 duction of finished works or exhibitions. The program runs from April to D
 ecember 2027 with a touchstone meeting in May 2027 and possible cohort con
 venings. Trio members must be regionally co-located anywhere in the United
  States so they can collaborate in person. The scientist should hold a Ph.
 D. and be conducting basic research\, with priority given to fields such a
 s astrophysics\, neuroscience\, quantum physics\, biology\, or mathematics
 . The application portal opens September 9\, 2026\, and all three trio mem
 bers must submit for the application to be complete.\n\nOrganisation: Simo
 ns Foundation\nLocation: United States (trio must be regionally co-located
 )\nAward: USD 30\,000 per awarded trio\nDuration: April to December 2027 (
 several months of collaboration)\n\nMore: https://www.simonsfoundation.org
 /2026/06/01/coming-soon-open-interval-an-artist-scientist-exploration-of-t
 urbulence/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.simonsfoundation.org/2026/06/01/coming-soon-open-interval-a
 n-artist-scientist-exploration-of-turbulence/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:United States (trio must be regionally co-located)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:helene-wurlitzer-foundation-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124023Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270119
SUMMARY:Deadline: Helene Wurlitzer Foundation Residency
DESCRIPTION:The Helene Wurlitzer Foundation of New Mexico runs one of the o
 ldest artist residency programs in the United States\, established in 1954
 \, on a 15-acre campus in Taos\, New Mexico. The residency is open to visu
 al artists\, literary artists\, and music composers\, including painters\,
  sculptors\, photographers\, filmmakers\, writers\, poets\, playwrights\, 
 screenwriters\, and songwriters. Selected grantees receive rent-free and u
 tility-paid housing in a furnished casita for a session of 10 to 12 weeks\
 , with access to a Commons House offering WiFi\, a library\, and bicycles.
  No stipend is provided in most cases\, and residents cover their own food
  and transportation. Applications are open to creative artists worldwide r
 egardless of age\, experience\, or nationality\, and the annual deadline i
 s January 18 for residencies the following calendar year. There is a non-w
 aivable USD 30 application fee.\n\nOrganisation: The Helene Wurlitzer Foun
 dation of New Mexico\nLocation: Taos\, New Mexico\, USA\nAward: Rent-free\
 , utility-paid furnished housing (casita)\; no stipend (rare stipend suppo
 rt via the Rhonda Artist Stipend Fund)\; artists cover food and travel USD
  30 application fee\nDuration: 10 to 12 weeks (Sessions 1 and 3 are 12 wee
 ks\, Session 2 is 10 weeks)\n\nMore: https://wurlitzerfoundation.org/apply
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://wurlitzerfoundation.org/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Taos\, New Mexico\, USA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:camargo-fellowship-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124023Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Camargo Foundation: Fellowship 2027-2028
DESCRIPTION:Founded by the artist and philanthropist Jerome Hill\, the Cama
 rgo Foundation has run this residency in Cassis on the Mediterranean coast
  since 1971\, and more than 1\,500 fellows have been through it. Fourteen 
 fellowships are awarded per cycle\, split roughly seven artists and seven 
 scholars or thinkers\, which is the point: the interdisciplinary cohort is
  the programme\, not a side effect. IMPORTANT: the Foundation has stated t
 hat this is the FINAL fellowship awarded through a public open call before
  it moves to a new selection process from 2027\, so if you have been meani
 ng to apply\, this is the cycle. RESEARCH\, NOT PRODUCTION: this is delibe
 rately structured as a research residency. You propose a project or line o
 f inquiry\, which can be development of a new work\, research preceding fu
 ture creative work\, or a broader investigation in your practice. Visual a
 rtists are explicitly reminded that research is prioritised over productio
 n\, and the Foundation supplies no art materials\, technical equipment or 
 artwork shipping\, so anything needing extensive fabrication is a poor fit
 . Fellows lead one resident session built around their own research or met
 hodology\, and attendance at these sessions is mandatory for everyone. Opt
 ional public Open Studios and introductions to organisations across the Ai
 x-Marseille-Provence region are also part of it. ELIGIBILITY: professional
  artists\, scholars and thinkers of any nationality. Artists should have a
 t least five years of professional practice and a mature body of work evid
 enced by exhibitions\, performances\, publications\, awards or grants. Per
 formance artists\, theatre directors\, choreographers\, multidisciplinary 
 artists\, writers\, filmmakers\, composers and visual artists are all elig
 ible within their categories. Collaborative applications of up to three me
 mbers are accepted. APPLICATION: four separate written responses covering 
 the project\, the research questions\, why Camargo specifically\, and why 
 now in your career\; reviewers are reading for a coherent research traject
 ory rather than a production proposal. An applicant webinar runs 1 Septemb
 er 2026. Deadline 1 October 2026 at 17:59 EST / 23:59 CET\; notifications 
 April 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Fondation Camargo\nLocation: Cassis\, France 
 (Mediterranean coast)\nAward: EUR 3\,500 stipend (EUR 350 per week for 10 
 weeks)\, basic transportation to and from Cassis\, a furnished apartment o
 n campus\, and a studio or appropriate workspace\, plus a reference librar
 y\, music and conference room and open-air theatre. Art materials\, techni
 cal equipment and shipping of artworks are NOT provided. No application fe
 e listed.\nDuration: Ten weeks. Fall 2027 session: 8 September to 17 Novem
 ber 2027. Spring 2028 session: 23 February to 4 May 2028.\n\nMore: https:/
 /camargofoundation.org/en/camargo-fellowship-2026-2027?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://camargofoundation.org/en/camargo-fellowship-2026-2027?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Cassis\, France (Mediterranean coast)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a4-residency-chengdu-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124023Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: A4 Residency Art Center: International Residency Programm
 e 2028 (Chengdu)
DESCRIPTION:Multidisciplinary international residency at the A4 Residency A
 rt Center in Chengdu\, China\, a global exchange platform integrating crea
 tion\, networking and resources\, dedicated to fostering cross-cultural cr
 eative collisions and innovation through residency programmes while promot
 ing deep integration of creative culture with commerce and communities. Re
 sidents initiate one to two participatory local activities to facilitate c
 ommunication with the city and community\; A4 also organises group activit
 ies\, intimate sharing and exhibition opportunities to foster understandin
 g among creators and connect them with local resources. AVAILABLE DATES: S
 pring 2028 (April - June) or Autumn 2028 (July - October). ELIGIBILITY: in
 ternational applicants from any field\; A4 welcomes applications from mult
 idisciplinary artists (visual\, performing\, music\, film\, sound\, archit
 ecture)\, curators\, designers (product\, fashion\, spatial\, interactive)
 \, and interdisciplinary creatives. PROGRAMME SUPPORT: studio and accommod
 ation\; round-trip economy airfare or 2nd-class train within a set budget\
 ; RMB 10\,000 production grant per person/team (excluding living expenses)
 . DEADLINE: 31 December 2026 (2028 cycles). APPLY via the A4 Residency Art
  Center latest-recruitment page.\n\nOrganisation: A4 Residency Art Center 
 (A4 Art Museum)\nLocation: Chengdu\, China\nAward: Studio and accommodatio
 n provided\; round-trip economy airfare or second-class train ticket withi
 n a set budget\; production grant of RMB 10\,000 per person/team for creat
 ive production and material costs (excluding living expenses). No applicat
 ion fee.\nDuration: No less than 8 weeks during one of two 2028 cycles: Sp
 ring 2028 (April - June) or Autumn 2028 (July - October)\n\nMore: https://
 www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyartcenter/residing/latest-recruitment/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyartcenter/residing/latest-re
 cruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Chengdu\, China
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:grand-canyon-conservancy-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124023Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260715
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260716
SUMMARY:Deadline: Grand Canyon Conservancy Residency 2027 (Artist / Astrono
 mer / Environmental Educator)
DESCRIPTION:Grand Canyon Conservancy's award-winning residency program invi
 tes artists\, scientists\, historians and educators to live on site at Gra
 nd Canyon National Park\, pursue place-based research\, and engage the pub
 lic through meaningful programs that deepen understanding of the park's en
 vironmental\, spiritual and cultural impact. Founded in 2020\; competitive
  application + peer-panel review. THREE TRACKS: (1) Artist in Residence - 
 for contemporary artists making interactive (immersive and/or participator
 y) work that shapes how people experience place\; (2) Astronomer in Reside
 nce - for astronomers from any discipline who wish to share their knowledg
 e and enthusiasm for dark skies\; (3) Environmental Educator in Residence 
 - for educators who use unique and inspiring methods to pique curiosity\, 
 prompt exploration\, and build knowledge of the world. Residents receive f
 ree accommodation\, financial support\, and marketing/exposure\; alumni re
 turn as part of a nationwide network. Read the individual track pages (lin
 ked from the main residency page) for track-specific eligibility\, session
  lengths\, stipend amounts\, public-engagement expectations and any region
 /citizenship requirements before applying. APPLICATIONS OPEN: 15 May - 15 
 July 2026 for the 2027 cycle.\n\nOrganisation: Grand Canyon Conservancy (G
 rand Canyon National Park)\nLocation: Grand Canyon National Park\, Arizona
 \, United States\nAward: Free on-site accommodation in the park\, financia
 l support (honorarium/stipend\; amount varies by track and session - confi
 rm on the track-specific page)\, plus marketing/exposure through the Conse
 rvancy and the National Park. Alumni network access. No application fee. T
 hree tracks (Artist / Astronomer / Environmental Educator) - apply to one 
 track per cycle.\nDuration: Place-based residency at Grand Canyon National
  Park during 2027\; dates and length vary by track\; residents are expecte
 d to engage the public through programs\, workshops\, talks or similar\n\n
 More: https://www.grandcanyon.org/experience-grand-canyon/residency-progra
 m?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.grandcanyon.org/experience-grand-canyon/residency-program?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Grand Canyon National Park\, Arizona\, United States
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pier-2-artist-in-residence-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124023Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260705
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260706
SUMMARY:Deadline: Pier-2 Art Center Artist-in-Residence Programme (PAIR) 20
 27 (Kaohsiung\, Taiwan)
DESCRIPTION:Pier-2 Artist-in-Residence Programme (PAIR) 2027 welcomes artis
 ts whose practice engages experimental approaches\, cross-disciplinary wor
 k\, and place-based research from Taiwan and abroad. Pier-2 Art Center is 
 a settlement-style arts hub in Kaohsiung\, transformed from former warehou
 se clusters\, known for diversity\, openness\, experimentation and innovat
 ion across visual arts\, music\, theatre\, cultural and creative industrie
 s\, film\, television\, and more. 2027 THEME: 'Beta Port | An Unfinished H
 arbour' - a state of becoming\; Beta Port suggests an unfixed\, in-progres
 s condition embodying openness\, fluidity and ongoing evolution\; An Unfin
 ished Harbour points to a city that continuously retains the potential to 
 be re-examined\, reconnected\, and rearticulated. PAIR approaches the resi
 dency as an open site of artistic production\, supporting artists to devel
 op works and methodologies in dialogue with Kaohsiung through research\, e
 xchange and practice. Artists are invited to take Kaohsiung as a starting 
 point and propose projects emphasising public engagement\, local sensibili
 ty\, and experimental approaches. ELIGIBILITY: open to artists and artisti
 c groups (of two people) of all nationalities with at least two years of e
 xperience in art creation. BENEFITS: studio and living space\; art exchang
 e opportunities\; round-trip economy flight or high-speed rail ticket\; da
 ily allowance of NTD 800 per person/group\; project material subsidy up to
  NTD 35\,000\; an assigned project manager. RESIDENCY 2027 PERIOD: 1 Janua
 ry - 31 December 2027 across four intervals (Jan-Mar\, Apr-Jun\, Jul-Sep\,
  Oct-Dec)\; each selected artist undertakes no less than 60 days and no mo
 re than 90 days. DEADLINE: 5 July 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Pier-2 Art Center
 \nLocation: Kaohsiung\, Taiwan (near the Port of Kaohsiung and the Love Ri
 ver estuary)\nAward: A 33 sqm studio with private bathroom plus 16.5 sqm l
 iving space\; art exchange area and opportunities\; one round-trip economy
  class flight ticket OR one round-trip reserved-seat high-speed rail ticke
 t (depending on artist's place of residence)\; daily living allowance of N
 TD 800 per person or group\; project-based material subsidy up to NTD 35\,
 000\; an assigned project manager. No application fee.\nDuration: 60 to 90
  days within one of four 2027 intervals: January-March\, April-June\, July
 -September\, or October-December\n\nMore: https://www.pier2air.tw/en/?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.pier2air.tw/en/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
LOCATION:Kaohsiung\, Taiwan (near the Port of Kaohsiung and the Love River 
 estuary)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:faber-andorra-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124023Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260713
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260714
SUMMARY:Deadline: Faber Andorra Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Individual interdisciplinary residency in La Massana\, Andorra\
 , in a natural mountain setting. ELIGIBILITY: open worldwide to any profes
 sional from the arts\, sciences and humanities with a project requiring fo
 cused working time\; visual and audiovisual arts\, crafts\, photography\, 
 dramaturgy\, performing arts\, cinema\, history\, curating\, criticism\, p
 hilosophy\, sociology\, anthropology\, journalism\, science\, research\, b
 iology\, ecology\, economics\, law\, writing and translation are all welco
 me. WHAT IS FUNDED: fully equipped apartment with work area\, optional 30 
 sqm visual and performing arts workshop\, and a daily allowance of EUR 60 
 to cover meals. Travel costs to/from Andorra and mandatory medical insuran
 ce are NOT covered. DURATION: 2 to 6 weeks\; stays scheduled between Febru
 ary and November 2027. RESIDENCY ACTIVITIES: residents must propose at lea
 st two activities to carry out during the stay (one aimed at school and/or
  university students)\; at least one activity must be executed. SELECTION:
  priority to projects related to Andorra and to activities most attractive
  to the Andorran community\; diversity of backgrounds and areas of work va
 lued\; previous Faberllull Olot/Faber Andorra residents may reapply but ne
 w candidates are preferred. APPLY: fill out the Faberllull form with a 1-p
 age cover letter and a 2-page proposal of two possible activities\; docume
 ntation accepted in Catalan\, Spanish\, English or French. TIMELINE: deadl
 ine 13 July 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Faberllull\nLocation: La Massana\, Ando
 rra\nAward: EUR 60 daily meal allowance plus fully equipped apartment (fre
 e) and 30 sqm visual/performing arts workshop. Travel and medical insuranc
 e NOT covered. No application fee.\nDuration: 2-6 weeks\, between February
  and November 2027\n\nMore: https://faberllull.cat/en/residencia.cfm?id=45
 820&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://faberllull.cat/en/residencia.cfm?id=45820&utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:La Massana\, Andorra
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:imera-postdoctoral-residency-2026-27@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124023Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260703
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260704
SUMMARY:Deadline: Iméra: 'This Is Not Another Fellowship' – Postdoctoral
  Residency 2026-27 (Aix-Marseille)
DESCRIPTION:Iméra's 'This Is Not Another Fellowship' is a 3-month postdoct
 oral residency at the Institute for Advanced Study at Aix Marseille Univer
 sité\, offered in two semester options: November 2\, 2026 – January 26\
 , 2027\, or March 1\, 2027 – May 28\, 2027. PROVIDED: free accommodation
  in one of fourteen campus apartments\; travel expenses covered\; desk in 
 shared open co-working space\; participation in the weekly Community Build
 ing Seminar (mandatory 3-hour Thursday sessions)\; access to interdiscipli
 nary scholarly networks. ELIGIBILITY: under 35 years old by May 28\, 2027\
 ; currently holding a postdoctoral fellowship contract at a university\; h
 ave not lived in France for more than 12 months in the prior 3 years\; if 
 requiring a visa\, must demonstrate sufficient funds. Research must align 
 with one of four Iméra programs: Arts & Sciences: Indisciplined Knowledge
 \; Interdisciplinary Dialogues\; Mediterranean\; or Necessary Utopias. All
  disciplines welcome. DEADLINE: 3 July 2026 at 1pm (CET+2). Apply at https
 ://www.imera.fr/en/this-is-not-another-fellowship-application-2026-27/.\n\
 nOrganisation: Iméra – Institute for Advanced Study at Aix Marseille Un
 iversité\nLocation: Aix-Marseille\, France (campus residency)\nAward: Fre
 e accommodation in campus apartment\; travel expenses covered\; office in 
 co-working space. No cash stipend specified. No application fee.\nDuration
 : 3 months: either November 2\, 2026 – January 26\, 2027\, or March 1\, 
 2027 – May 28\, 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.imera.fr/en/this-is-not-anoth
 er-fellowship-application-2026-27/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.imera.fr/en/this-is-not-another-fellowship-application-2026
 -27/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Aix-Marseille\, France (campus residency)
